<title>UK: Northern in deal to power Sainsbury.</title>
<headline>Northern in deal to power Sainsbury.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Electricity said it has won a contract to supply 1,350 GWh of electricity to power all of supermarket chain J. Sainsbury's premises in England and Wales for a year from November 1.</p>
<p>Northern said competition for the contract had been intense but did not give any financial details.</p>
<p>Northern is the subject of a 630p per share hostile takeover bid from CalEnergy Co Inc's CE Electric. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
